<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Armenia</h1><p class="st-meta">653 CE – 884 CE (approx.) · capital Dvin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Armenia under Arab rule, when native princes governed beside the caliph's governor at Dvin and the Bagratid family rose towards kingship.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As Arab armies overran the Sasanian lands, the Armenian commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-rshtuni">Theodore Rshtuni</a> made a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Muawiya</a> in 653 accepting Arab overlordship in return for autonomy and keeping Armenian troops. The province of Arminiya, which also took in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>, was established with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>An Arab governor, the ostikan, sat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a> while a native presiding prince represented the Armenian nobility. Heavy taxes provoked revolts, notably in 774-775, which were crushed and weakened the Mamikonian house. Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> settled in towns, while monasteries preserved Armenian learning. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagratuni-dynasty">Bagratids</a> grew rich through lands and trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> weakening, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashot-i-of-armenia">Ashot Bagratuni</a> was named prince of princes in 862, and around 884 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> sent him a crown, founding <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bagratid-armenia">Bagratid Armenia</a>. The period had preserved the noble houses, the church and a sense of separate identity that made this revival of Armenian kingship possible.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 653 CE – 884 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Caucasus</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:72.70%;width:4.60%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>653 CE – 884 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dvin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Theodore Rshtuni, Ashot Msaker, Ashot I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Armenian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Armenian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arminiya, Presiding Princes of Armenia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=768&amp;focus=principality-of-armenia" aria-label="Principality of Armenia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5777 746 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Armenia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6097 1002L5972 1046M6097 1002L6097 1002M6097 1002L6053 1533M6097 1002L6134 1224M6097 1002L6134 1224M6097 1002L6069 986"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5972 1046h0M6097 1002h0M6053 1533h0M6134 1224h0M6134 1224h0M6069 986h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6097 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6097 1002h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dvin. <a href="/atlas?year=768&amp;focus=principality-of-armenia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
